{1}{Thank Alberich you found us! We were liable to starve in there. Damned zombies. You made short work of them, though, eh?}{Thank Alberich you found us! We were liable to starve in there. Damned zombies. You made short work of them, though, eh?}{}{}{}{}
{2}{What happened here?}{}{5}{}{50}{lf5 1}
{3}{I'm looking for Erland Iron Heart. Do you know him?}{}{5}{qa1091 1}{10}{lf1 1}
{10}{Of course I know him. I'm him.}{Of course I know him. I'm him.}{}{}{}{}
{11}{Your brother sent me to ask you to go home.}{}{5}{}{20}{}
{20}{[He shakes his head.] Thrayne, poor Thrayne. He's been so overprotective of me since our father died. He blames himself for it, you know.}{[He shakes his head.] Thrayne, poor Thrayne. He's been so overprotective of me since our father died. He blames himself for it, you know.}{}{}{}{gf2195 1}
{21}{What happened to your father?}{}{5}{}{30}{}
{22}{So are you going to go home?}{}{5}{}{40}{}
{23}{What happened here?}{}{5}{lf5 0}{50}{lf5 1}
{30}{I'd rather not speak of it anymore. I'd best be on my way home so that my dear brother doesn't worry himself to death.}{I'd rather not speak of it anymore. I'd best be on my way home so that my dear brother doesn't worry himself to death.}{}{}{}{qu1091 4}
{31}{What happened here?}{}{5}{lf5 0}{50}{lf5 1}
{40}{I suppose I had better. I was planning on leaving for home soon, anyway, before this all happened. [He looks around.] And I don't think I'm welcome around here anymore.}{I suppose I had better. I was planning on leaving for home soon, anyway, before this all happened. [He looks around.] And I don't think I'm welcome around here anymore.}{}{}{}{qu1091 4}
{41}{What happened here?}{}{5}{lf5 0}{50}{lf5 1}
{49}{I'd best be on my way.}{}{5}{}{0}{lf2 1}
{50}{[He chuckles softly, and looks at his shoes a bit sheepishly.] I would, ah, be responsible for all this. I found an ancient necromancer's laboratory off an old, abandoned access cavern. In researching his journals, I deduced a way to reproduce what he had done through magick by using scientific principles.}{[He chuckles softly, and looks at his shoes a bit sheepishly.] I would, ah, be responsible for all this. I found an ancient necromancer's laboratory off an old, abandoned access cavern. In researching his journals, I deduced a way to reproduce what he had done through magick by using scientific principles.}{}{}{}{ru2137}
{51}{So you created all these zombies? That was a bit irresponsible.}{}{5}{}{60}{}
{52}{Where is this laboratory?}{}{5}{}{70}{lf3 1}
{60}{I assure you it was an accident. The first one I created began an awful, horrific screeching, and flailing about. It knocked over my chemicals and before I knew what was happening they were coming out of the floor. They were everywhere! Luckily, I was able to get back here to warn everyone.}{I assure you it was an accident. The first one I created began an awful, horrific screeching, and flailing about. It knocked over my chemicals and before I knew what was happening they were coming out of the floor. They were everywhere! Luckily, I was able to get back here to warn everyone.}{}{}{}{}
